1
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:13,340
Lighten up your room and try stepping away.

2
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:26,880
Aiming for the spring sun
floating on the Naka River,

3
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:33,980
I kicked a pebble and even my shoe flew off.

4
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:42,260
onto the head of the carpenter
who was in a chokehold.

5
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:48,440
They laughed at me for staying a kid.

6
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:53,540
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,

7
00:00:53,540 --> 00:00:58,620
Pachinko Kameari, one yawn,
and nothing changes.

8
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:02,520
The streets are strangely gentle.

9
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:10,520
From the pointed hat's water basin,

10
00:01:11,140 --> 00:01:16,780
the sunset falls into the vast sky.

11
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow will end just like this, won't it.

12
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:29,060
Katsushika, Shibamata,
happiness again, they say.

13
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:33,840
I kept going out and realized,
because I'm such a fool.

14
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:41,000
Desperate straits, the end of the road

15
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:47,140
Settled in 1 hour! Settled in 1 hour!

16
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:52,460
BGPTG4 Settled in 1 hour! Settled in 1 hour!

17
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:58,020
Welcome! Welcome!

18
00:02:00,060 --> 00:02:02,560
Kameari's fun cabaret, Miss Kameari

19
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:05,100
Safe and secure with accounting,
Miss Kameari

20
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:07,080
We operate on a fully prepaid system.

21
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:11,180
Come on, how about it, sir?
Why don't you stay and play?

22
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:12,300
But I...

23
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:14,220
Sir, this isn't our place, you know.

24
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:16,020
Put it on the bill.

25
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:17,380
What is it?

26
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:20,340
Me, me, let's have some fun.

27
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:22,160
Yes, one guest, this way.

28
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:24,700
Hey, I won't do anything naughty, I promise.

29
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:28,200
Understood, Section Chief.
I understand, I said.

30
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:32,800
Aren't you stressed out from work?

31
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:35,920
Yeah, I'm totally stressed out.

32
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:39,020
One look at your face and I can tell you're a real piece of work,
you know.

33
00:02:39,020 --> 00:02:41,600
Saying your ability's pretty poor,
or something like that!

34
00:02:42,060 --> 00:02:45,180
So you're saying as long as ability goes up,
quality doesn't matter?

35
00:02:45,180 --> 00:02:46,320
You bastard!

36
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:49,060
Right, so in that case,
let's get rid of all that built-up stress -

37
00:02:49,060 --> 00:02:51,440
Why not let it all out here at our place?
How about it?

38
00:02:51,440 --> 00:02:52,660
So cute, so cute.

39
00:02:52,660 --> 00:02:55,340
Of course, we've got plenty of busty
gals swarming all over the place.

40
00:02:55,340 --> 00:02:56,480
Busty!

41
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:58,540
Alright, then Ikeda-kun, next -

42
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:00,400
Don't mind if I do.

43
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:02,760
Alright, you two, this way, please.

44
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:07,340
Yes, yes, welcome, customer!

45
00:03:08,940 --> 00:03:13,440
Chief, Chief, you come to places like this?
That's surprising.

46
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:17,480
We're an honest, transparent-pricing establishment,
so, please, come on in!

47
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:19,860
Idiot, I didn't come here as a customer!

48
00:03:19,860 --> 00:03:25,360
I got a report that someone in a police uniform was touting,
so I came, and it's you after all!

49
00:03:26,460 --> 00:03:28,700
What on earth do you think you're doing?!

50
00:03:30,060 --> 00:03:33,660
A part-time job?
Why are you claiming it's a part-time job?

51
00:03:33,660 --> 00:03:38,360
Because Ryo-san has to work a part-time
job to cover his living expenses.

52
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:42,380
That's because you blow all your money on games,
radio-controlled toys, and the like!

53
00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:45,900
No, well, I have my own reasons, you know.

54
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:47,160
Shut up, you Marikon...

55
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:50,440
If the Chief finds us here,
my section is in trouble.

56
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:51,580
Just come with me.

57
00:03:51,580 --> 00:03:53,820
W-wait, please, just one more hour...

58
00:03:53,820 --> 00:03:56,980
If I don't work one more hour,
I won't get my part-time pay.

59
00:03:56,980 --> 00:03:59,240
Shut up, you super problem child.

60
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:03,060
What? You're touting for
a cabaret during duty hours?

61
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:04,480
In this outfit?

62
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:07,720
Ryo-sama,
even though you have me right here...

63
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:11,240
Working somewhere with so many
women like that is indecent.

64
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:14,820
Don't you have any sense of
responsibility as a police officer?

65
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:17,680
I-I'm no different,
I'm no different either...

66
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:20,760
I'm not doing this because I want to.

67
00:04:22,020 --> 00:04:25,660
It's tough, really tough, this life of mine.

68
00:04:25,660 --> 00:04:27,920
At this rate, I, I...

69
00:04:27,970 --> 00:04:30,280
I'm going to starve to death!

70
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:36,120
Poor Ryo-sama.

71
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:38,360
Do you understand, Maria?

72
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:40,920
But part-time work violates
the service regulations,

73
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:44,220
and if you keep it up,
you could really get fired.

74
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:46,780
I'll die if I don't work part-time,
so it can't be helped, right?

75
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:51,660
If I starve to death,
I'll haunt your pillow, Chief.

76
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:54,760
If you need money that badly,

77
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:56,440
why don't you work here at the station?

78
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,980
Like doing overtime,

79
00:04:58,980 --> 00:05:01,280
or helping with desk work.
How about it, Ryotsu?

80
00:05:01,660 --> 00:05:02,560
Here at the station?

81
00:05:03,540 --> 00:05:05,740
But needs must in this case.

82
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:07,840
I'll do it! I'll do it! Please let me!

83
00:05:08,260 --> 00:05:10,120
Chief, you're my lifesaver.

84
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:12,640
Don't be so dramatic.

85
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:15,580
That way, I can rest easy too.

86
00:05:15,580 --> 00:05:19,180
Ryotsu Kankichi, I will never forget this kindness,
not until I forget it.

87
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:21,700
Easy, easy.

88
00:05:33,300 --> 00:05:35,240
Part-time work,
and it's just washing patrol cars?

89
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:37,480
And that's per car, waxing included.

90
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:39,560
That only comes to 360 yen

91
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:41,280
Man, this is sickening.

92
00:05:41,660 --> 00:05:44,420
On top of that,
I have to fill up the gas tanks too.

93
00:05:44,940 --> 00:05:47,840
Moving them over there one
at a time is such a pain.

94
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:50,360
Oh, right!

95
00:06:00,660 --> 00:06:03,380
Wow, I'm so brilliant!

96
00:06:07,260 --> 00:06:08,500
Hold on a sec!

97
00:06:10,140 --> 00:06:12,000
Ryotsu, Kankichi!

98
00:06:12,180 --> 00:06:13,940
That's dangerous!
You'll end up in the afterlife, you know!

99
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:19,780
Aren't you thoughtful.

100
00:06:19,780 --> 00:06:23,380
Has the most hated man around
finally changed his ways a little?

101
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,400
Here are your hand towels and fruit platter.

102
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:27,540
Thanks.

103
00:06:27,540 --> 00:06:28,740
Looks delicious, doesn't it?

104
00:06:35,060 --> 00:06:37,120
Well, here is your bill.

105
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:38,300
The bill.

106
00:06:39,020 --> 00:06:43,100
With tax included, it comes to 15,750 yen.

107
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:44,960
What is this?!

108
00:06:45,180 --> 00:06:47,120
There's no way I can pay this!

109
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:49,570
So you won't be paying, then.

110
00:06:49,620 --> 00:06:52,000
Well, this is a problem, sir.

111
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:55,380
My colleague here says you
absolutely refuse to pay.

112
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:58,778
You had the girls
serving you all night long,

113
00:06:58,828 --> 00:07:02,620
and now you're saying you won't pay?
Isn't that a bit too convenient for you?

114
00:07:03,100 --> 00:07:03,603
Yeah.

115
00:07:03,653 --> 00:07:07,340
Come on, pay up while we're
still being nice about it.

116
00:07:09,840 --> 00:07:11,860
Idiot! You're the worst!

117
00:07:11,860 --> 00:07:14,060
Don't be ridiculous, you octopus!

118
00:07:14,060 --> 00:07:15,780
You stinking poet!

119
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:17,820
Don't go doing a one-man comedy routine!

120
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:19,820
Damn it, he skipped out on the bill!

121
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:21,540
You'll pay for this, damn you!

122
00:07:24,260 --> 00:07:25,060
Chief.

123
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:27,740
Ryotsu, what were you just doing?

124
00:07:27,740 --> 00:07:30,400
You were watching, Chief?
You're a sneaky one.

125
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:32,300
If you're going to be here, at least say so!

126
00:07:32,300 --> 00:07:33,560
You idiot!

127
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:35,300
What kind of man are you?

128
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:37,660
Trying to pull off a fake cabaret
touting scheme inside the station?

129
00:07:37,660 --> 00:07:39,120
You colossal idiot!

130
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,106
But...

131
00:07:40,156 --> 00:07:44,560
Three hundred sixty yen per car,
and that's supposed to cover my living...

132
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:47,320
Shut up! No arguments!

133
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:55,560
Damn it!

134
00:07:56,620 --> 00:07:58,260
The g-gasoline...

135
00:07:59,060 --> 00:08:00,800
Pyotsu! Restrain him!

136
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:06,800
Gasoline! That's absolutely not allowed!
Hey! It's just me alone...

137
00:08:21,020 --> 00:08:22,300
Aaaaaaah

138
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:23,100
Aaaaaaah

139
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:24,440
Aaaaaaah

140
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:25,260
Aaaaaaah

141
00:08:25,260 --> 00:08:25,640
Aaaaaaah

142
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:26,120
Aaaaaaah

143
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:27,460
Aaaaaaah

144
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:27,480
Aaaaaaah

145
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:29,560
Aaaaaaah

146
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:33,400
Excuse me! Sorry to interrupt!

147
00:08:34,040 --> 00:08:35,680
Pardon the intrusion, ta-da!

148
00:08:59,820 --> 00:09:02,460
Ohara, what is the meaning of this?

149
00:09:03,340 --> 00:09:04,800
It's all because that Ryotsu -

150
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:06,420
What are you talking about?

151
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:08,780
Well, the Chief threw
me across the room first!

152
00:09:08,780 --> 00:09:09,660
What did you say?

153
00:09:09,660 --> 00:09:11,420
You did such a thing, so I -

154
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:12,300
What are you talking about?

155
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:15,920
Well, the Chief makes me write so
many incident reports that my bonus -

156
00:09:15,920 --> 00:09:19,720
You cause incidents, so you have to
write incident reports, you idiot!

157
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:22,820
Calling people idiots is the only trick you know,
you idiot!

158
00:09:22,820 --> 00:09:24,620
What's wrong with calling an idiot an idiot?

159
00:09:24,620 --> 00:09:26,740
You're a guaranteed idiot, you know that!

160
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:28,980
Stop it, you pair of idiots!

161
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:32,520
You're both responsible!
You two will take the blame for this!

162
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:36,100
Ryo-sama and Chief Ohara are
being reassigned to a remote post?!

163
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:39,566
That's right! To take responsibility
for wrecking the Katsushika station,

164
00:09:39,616 --> 00:09:41,680
both the Chief and Ryo-san have
been demoted to ordinary officers!

165
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:44,160
On top of that,
they're both being transferred!

166
00:09:44,660 --> 00:09:46,820
Well, you got off pretty lightly.

167
00:09:46,870 --> 00:09:49,080
I was worried they'd fire him.

168
00:09:49,820 --> 00:09:53,780
I'll always bring a bento
when I come to visit Ryo-sama!

169
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:55,080
That's impossible.

170
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:56,340
Why not?

171
00:09:56,880 --> 00:09:59,420
The place they're being
transferred to is a bit of a problem.

172
00:09:59,980 --> 00:10:00,300
A problem?

173
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:02,460
If I had to go to a place like that,

174
00:10:02,460 --> 00:10:04,420
I'd have rather been fired.

175
00:10:05,300 --> 00:10:06,700
So where exactly are the two of them going?

176
00:10:08,540 --> 00:10:09,580
It's Saihate-sho, you know.

177
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:11,040
Eeh!

178
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:13,100
Saihate-sho, wasn't that

179
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:13,480
Yeah.

180
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:16,400
Saihate-sho is a phantom island
that isn't even on the map.

181
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:19,160
It's the legendary police
box on Saihate Island.

182
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:24,320
The island is surrounded by sheer cliffs,

183
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:25,840
and you can't even get close by boat.

184
00:10:26,340 --> 00:10:30,340
They say that once you go to that remote sea,
you'll never come back alive.

185
00:10:44,820 --> 00:10:47,000
Wasn't there a Tsuchinoko just now?

186
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:51,040
Either way, it's a jungle no
one has set foot in for decades.

187
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:53,920
It wouldn't be strange if
Tsuchinoko or dinosaurs showed up.

188
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:09,900
This is Saihate-sho.

189
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:30,880
Wow, this is incredible.

190
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:33,300
It's like a dream.

191
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:36,020
Can people actually live
in a place like this?

192
00:11:37,160 --> 00:11:38,360
Look at all this dust.

193
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:41,100
It's the logbook.

194
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:44,540
The last date is

195
00:11:45,400 --> 00:11:47,440
recorded as Taisho 10.

196
00:11:59,460 --> 00:12:02,040
No one's going to come anyway,
so let's take it easy.

197
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:06,780
Don't be ridiculous. We don't have time to play around.
First, we have to do the handover.

198
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:08,320
Handover? Handover to whom?

199
00:12:09,640 --> 00:12:11,840
Then let's decide the patrol rotation.

200
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:15,620
If you go out alone,
you might get lost and never make it back.

201
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:18,220
Then we'll do a residents' survey.

202
00:12:18,220 --> 00:12:20,980
It's an uninhabited island.
The only ones living here are the two of us.

203
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:24,600
Then what are the two of us supposed to do?

204
00:12:26,340 --> 00:12:27,820
Then let me teach you.

205
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:32,220
The very first thing to do when
living on a desert island is,

206
00:12:32,220 --> 00:12:32,940
it's,

207
00:12:32,940 --> 00:12:34,960
it's securing drinking water.

208
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:35,540
Drinking water.

209
00:12:35,540 --> 00:12:38,520
To survive, humans first need water.

210
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:42,380
On an island this size, there should
certainly be a spring or a stream.

211
00:12:42,380 --> 00:12:44,900
Finding it is the top priority.

212
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:48,260
I see, well, I'm learning something here.

213
00:12:48,260 --> 00:12:51,020
Alright, then water, go fetch water, Ryotsu!

214
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:54,600
What do you mean,
"huh"? I'm talking to you, Ryotsu!

215
00:12:56,560 --> 00:13:05,720
No, Chief, Ohara-kun, you've already been demoted to
the same rank as a regular patrol officer, Ohara-kun.

216
00:13:05,720 --> 00:13:08,320
Stop giving me orders every little thing,
will you?

217
00:13:10,580 --> 00:13:15,320
We're both regular officers now, so we
should share everything equally, Ohara-kun.

218
00:13:17,180 --> 00:13:19,260
Fine, let's go, just the two of us.

219
00:13:26,820 --> 00:13:29,960
Is this way really all right, Ryotsu-kun?

220
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:32,840
If you don't like it,
you can go on your own, Ohara-kun.

221
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:34,260
No, no, I would never...

222
00:13:35,060 --> 00:13:37,380
Wait! Don't leave me alone, Ryotsu!

223
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:40,180
No, Ryotsu-kun, wait! Ryotsu-kun!

224
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:57,300
When it comes to survival like this,
I'm counting on you.

225
00:13:57,980 --> 00:13:58,620
You?

226
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:01,940
No, I mean Ryotsu-kun, Ryotsu-kun.

227
00:14:02,580 --> 00:14:04,280
I'm counting on Ryotsu-kun.

228
00:14:06,620 --> 00:14:08,060
What's wrong, Ryotsu-kun?

229
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:11,840
Nothing, I can faintly hear
water beyond these bushes.

230
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:12,640
Right, let's go.

231
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:14,420
Wait, Ryotsu-kun!

232
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:14,880
Whoa!

233
00:14:15,140 --> 00:14:16,540
Ow ow

234
00:14:23,820 --> 00:14:24,520
This is

235
00:14:25,640 --> 00:14:26,280
a lake.

236
00:14:28,220 --> 00:14:31,280
But it's strangely eerily quiet, isn't it?

237
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:35,600
It feels like Nessie
could show up any moment.

238
00:14:38,140 --> 00:14:39,760
Something's coming out, Ryotsu-kun!

239
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:40,960
So it really is Nessie after all?

240
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:44,040
No, this is the Saihate Island,
so it's Saihate-Nessie!

241
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:50,360
Tch, what a letdown.

242
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:51,740
It's just a tree!

243
00:14:51,740 --> 00:14:54,320
Let's hurry up,
fill the water and head back, Ohara-kun.

244
00:14:54,320 --> 00:14:55,180
Let's do that.

245
00:14:56,240 --> 00:14:58,280
Ohara-kun, about this bucket...

246
00:14:58,280 --> 00:15:01,660
Let's play rock-paper-scissors,
and the loser carries it 500 steps each.

247
00:15:01,660 --> 00:15:03,020
Rock, paper, scissors!

248
00:15:03,020 --> 00:15:03,740
You don't want to?

249
00:15:03,740 --> 00:15:04,420
No, that's not...

250
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:08,920
497

251
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:10,200
498

252
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:11,220
499

253
00:15:11,940 --> 00:15:12,660
500, and

254
00:15:14,040 --> 00:15:16,660
Janken, janken, janken, pon!

255
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:20,000
I won again! Well, let's go.

256
00:15:21,100 --> 00:15:24,280
Hey, Ryotsu-kun,
could you let me rest a little longer?

257
00:15:24,280 --> 00:15:26,980
Fine. Just a little.

258
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:34,300
Typhoon No.
17, a large and very powerful typhoon,

259
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:38,460
is gradually shifting its course eastward and
is expected to approach the Japanese archipelago.

260
00:15:38,460 --> 00:15:42,280
If it keeps on this course, the
typhoon will hit Saihate Island directly.

261
00:15:59,140 --> 00:16:01,100
It looks like a pretty strong typhoon.

262
00:16:01,100 --> 00:16:02,860
Can this rickety shack really hold up?

263
00:16:02,860 --> 00:16:05,140
Well, I did reinforce it for now.

264
00:16:06,140 --> 00:16:07,480
As expected of you, Ryotsu-kun.

265
00:16:07,480 --> 00:16:08,820
You're really reliable.

266
00:16:08,820 --> 00:16:11,000
Anyway, the real problem is this.

267
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:14,480
After searching everywhere,
this is all we could find to eat.

268
00:16:14,980 --> 00:16:16,720
Speaking of which, I'm starving.

269
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:18,680
I haven't eaten a thing
since we got to this island.

270
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:21,660
But if we give in to our
cravings and eat everything,

271
00:16:21,660 --> 00:16:24,160
our food will run out in no time.

272
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:25,340
Th-that's true.

273
00:16:25,340 --> 00:16:29,120
Let's pool all the food we
each brought into one place,

274
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:32,500
and then share it out fairly, little by little.
I think that's best.

275
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:34,300
I see. That's a sound argument.

276
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:38,320
I only have this much.

277
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,260
This is all I have.

278
00:16:42,260 --> 00:16:43,340
What is this?

279
00:16:43,340 --> 00:16:45,440
It's nothing but manga and model kits!

280
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:46,300
That's rough.

281
00:16:46,300 --> 00:16:49,360
Look, there's a can of food.

282
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:52,060
And one piece of candy.

283
00:16:52,060 --> 00:16:53,220
Is that all?

284
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:57,580
Okay, that's all the food we have, then.

285
00:16:57,580 --> 00:17:00,520
Most of this is the food I brought,
isn't it?

286
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:03,560
So, our disaster gear
is fine for now, right?

287
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:04,540
And the rest?

288
00:17:04,540 --> 00:17:05,260
And the rest?

289
00:17:05,260 --> 00:17:08,760
To avoid wasting energy and getting hungry,

290
00:17:08,760 --> 00:17:10,140
sleeping is the best thing to do.

291
00:17:45,420 --> 00:17:47,740
I'm so hungry I can't stand it.

292
00:17:47,740 --> 00:17:54,380
And that was it.

293
00:17:54,380 --> 00:17:58,980
Well then.

294
00:17:58,980 --> 00:18:06,620
So I knew it would come to this!
No, I was just going to check what's inside.

295
00:18:06,620 --> 00:18:08,220
I can't believe that!

296
00:18:08,560 --> 00:18:10,920
Put this as far away from you as possible.

297
00:18:14,460 --> 00:18:14,860
What?

298
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:18,420
Be careful, Ryotsu!

299
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:29,400
Ryotsu!

300
00:18:36,620 --> 00:18:39,300
Chief! This shack is half over the sea!

301
00:18:39,940 --> 00:18:40,660
What!?

302
00:18:40,660 --> 00:18:44,020
It could tip over and fall
into the sea at any moment!

303
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:53,140
We don't have time to rest, Ryotsu!
Hurry over here!

304
00:19:06,620 --> 00:19:07,540
Aaaaaaah!

305
00:19:07,540 --> 00:19:10,340
Aaaaaaah!

306
00:19:15,020 --> 00:19:18,240
Eeeeeeek!

307
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:21,720
Aaaaaaah!

308
00:19:21,720 --> 00:19:27,440
Eeeeeeek!

309
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:33,740
Eeeeeeek!

310
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:44,420
What are we going to do now, Ryotsu?

311
00:19:44,420 --> 00:19:45,920
Look, Chief.

312
00:19:45,920 --> 00:19:49,480
The floor to that far door
is about four meters long.

313
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:52,280
That's about the distance two
people reach when lying end to end.

314
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:52,840
I see.

315
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:54,380
Alright, bring it on!

316
00:20:08,520 --> 00:20:09,520
Ryotsu

317
00:20:09,520 --> 00:20:12,740
But I slipped,
so it can't be helped, can it?

318
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:15,380
Next time, I'm on top, got it?

319
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:16,820
Fine, fine, I get it.

320
00:20:17,420 --> 00:20:18,380
Here you go.

321
00:20:22,240 --> 00:20:23,680
We did it, Ryotsu!

322
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:26,500
Right, then hold on tight, will you?

323
00:20:26,500 --> 00:20:31,260
Oof, you're heavy!
Why did you come along too?

324
00:20:31,260 --> 00:20:32,940
Come on, what's the big deal?

325
00:20:33,800 --> 00:20:34,820
Yay!

326
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:42,020
No, once more!

327
00:20:42,020 --> 00:20:42,520
Mm.

328
00:20:46,180 --> 00:20:47,880
Aaaaaaah!

329
00:20:48,640 --> 00:20:53,160
Aaaaaaah! Once more!

330
00:20:53,160 --> 00:20:54,380
Aaaaaaah!

331
00:20:54,380 --> 00:21:00,660
Aaaaaaah! Once more!

332
00:21:00,660 --> 00:21:02,860
Aaaaaaah!

333
00:21:09,700 --> 00:21:13,180
If both of us go over there at once,
the weight will make it tip over.

334
00:21:13,180 --> 00:21:14,980
First, one of us should step outside.

335
00:21:14,980 --> 00:21:18,440
This is your fault for climbing up like that,
you know!

336
00:21:18,440 --> 00:21:20,460
Fine, fine, I get it already!

337
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:27,500
Looks like it's safe.

338
00:21:36,320 --> 00:21:37,260
What's wrong?

339
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:40,880
Idiot! Get back!

340
00:21:40,960 --> 00:21:41,860
This way!

341
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:43,800
Chief, what should I do?

342
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:45,040
Don't come over here!

343
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:46,520
Then, here's the bag, there you go!

344
00:21:46,580 --> 00:21:47,560
I don't need it!

345
00:21:47,620 --> 00:21:48,300
Here, Chief!

346
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:49,320
I don't want it!

347
00:21:49,680 --> 00:21:50,900
Here! Here!

348
00:21:51,340 --> 00:21:52,020
With this, look!

349
00:21:52,120 --> 00:21:52,680
I'm giving it to you!

350
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:53,280
I don't want it!

351
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:05,840
You mustn't move!

352
00:22:05,840 --> 00:22:07,000
You're the one moving, Chief!

353
00:22:14,420 --> 00:22:17,180
All that moving has made me starving.

354
00:22:17,180 --> 00:22:19,180
I'm so hungry I'm going to die.

355
00:22:19,180 --> 00:22:21,400
Chief, let's eat, let's eat!

356
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:22,920
I can't hold out any longer.

357
00:22:22,920 --> 00:22:25,380
Just go back! Do you really want to die?

358
00:22:26,160 --> 00:22:28,680
But Chief,
if we stay like this and can't move...

359
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:30,820
We'll really starve to death!

360
00:22:30,820 --> 00:22:34,380
I'm hungry too. I want to eat.

361
00:22:34,760 --> 00:22:38,520
Fine, here's what we'll do. Let's both step closer,
one step at a time, at the same moment.

362
00:22:38,600 --> 00:22:40,040
That way, our balance won't break.

363
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:42,440
Right, let's do that.

364
00:22:44,300 --> 00:22:44,980
Ready... go!

365
00:22:45,120 --> 00:22:45,380
Ready... go!

366
00:22:46,140 --> 00:22:48,820
One, two,

367
00:22:49,520 --> 00:22:52,900
Whoa! Hey, Ryotsu!
Your steps are way too big!

368
00:22:53,020 --> 00:22:54,040
This one's mine too!

369
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:57,800
Hand it over! Most of this is mine anyway!

370
00:22:57,960 --> 00:22:58,980
I said hand it over, got it?

371
00:23:19,380 --> 00:23:22,740
Wow, the weather's cleared up
as if yesterday never happened.

372
00:23:23,220 --> 00:23:24,980
Truly a typhoon family

373
00:23:24,980 --> 00:23:27,220
Ryo-sama, are you all right?

374
00:23:31,780 --> 00:23:34,420
It's biting! Yes, I caught one!

375
00:23:34,420 --> 00:23:36,220
Chief, share some with me too!

376
00:23:36,220 --> 00:23:38,740
This is mine! I caught it!

377
00:23:38,740 --> 00:23:40,960
Don't be so stingy about it.

378
00:23:40,960 --> 00:23:46,280
And it's been so long since
we've had a proper meal.

379
00:23:46,280 --> 00:23:48,140
It's your fault for being so stingy, Chief.

380
00:23:48,140 --> 00:23:50,620
What? It's you who's the
one who's taking my catch!

381
00:23:53,080 --> 00:23:54,820
Let's stop, we'll only get hungrier.

382
00:23:55,380 --> 00:23:56,180
Yeah, you're right.

383
00:23:56,881 --> 00:24:00,620
Compared to this,
Saihate Station was still better.

384
00:24:04,280 --> 00:24:06,800
Everyone, thank you so much
for your long-standing support.

385
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:08,920
Starting next week, a new show

386
00:24:08,920 --> 00:24:11,140
Hard-Boiled Zega is about to begin!

387
00:24:11,140 --> 00:24:11,840
Who's that?!

388
00:24:12,120 --> 00:24:13,500
The one who wrote this manuscript

389
00:24:13,500 --> 00:24:15,700
Kochikame isn't over yet!

390
00:24:15,700 --> 00:24:16,860
What? What?

391
00:24:17,040 --> 00:24:18,900
Next time, I'm the star!

392
00:24:18,900 --> 00:24:20,020
Hoshi Tōden

393
00:24:20,020 --> 00:24:21,080
So it's you!

394
00:24:37,280 --> 00:24:43,660
Light blending,
quick problem-solving, lending a hand

395
00:24:43,660 --> 00:24:55,300
Decided by inspiration, bouncing,
gathering it up, action, flying off

396
00:24:56,360 --> 00:24:59,980
Above all, power in sumo!

397
00:24:59,980 --> 00:25:12,240
Everyone, gather!
Come here, and the dreamlike final energy

398
00:25:13,340 --> 00:25:23,420
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday, painting the universe,
standing on the ground, the star of Kameari spun around in a circle

399
00:25:25,500 --> 00:25:28,640
"Is this good enough?" "Like hell it is!"

400
00:25:36,820 --> 00:25:40,140
Thank you for watching.

